    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d441">

                <pb facs="0568" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg483"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/979: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-12T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 12,
                                1919, 2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>9101. Department’s 9094, September 8, 6 p.m. Your 1368 Sept. 8. 8 P.M.<anchor
                        n="26" xml:id="d441-f1"/> Following received from French Embassy, dated
                    September 5:</p>
                <pb facs="0569" n="484" xml:id="pg484"/>
                <p>[Here follows the note printed on <ref target="#pg481">page 481</ref>.]</p>
                <p>French Ambassador is being informed that this Government does not consider
                    negotiations as terminated and has in fact asked you to convey final views of
                    this Government with a request for early reply. As these views which were
                    communicated to French Ambassador in Department’s memorandum of November 19,
                    1918, provide for an exclusive American Receivership, this Government is not in
                    a position to accede to the wishes of French Government in this matter.</p>
                <p>You may orally inform French Foreign Office in above sense adding that under the
                    terms of the Bankers Contract of 1912 Liberia is in position to purchase
                    outstanding 5 percent bonds with advances to be made by United States Treasury
                    thereby automatically putting an end to French share in Receivership. See
                    Department’s 2432, June 26 to Ammission and reply of Ammission 3315, July 25, 8
                        p.m.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d441-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
